# 0x06 — CORRELATION & ANALYSIS TRADECRAFT

This is where raw data becomes actual intelligence:

| Technique | Worked Example |
|---|---|
| **Username pivoting** | A GitHub commit by `jdoe_dev` leads to a Twitter/X account with the same handle, which links to a personal blog revealing the person's real name and employer — now you have a phishing pretext with real personal detail. |
| **Email → breach → password pattern** | `jsmith@target.com` appears in 3 breaches, each showing a variation of the same base password (`Summer2021!`, `Summer2022!`) — revealing a seasonal password-rotation habit worth testing (in an authorized password-spray, never against live prod without scope). |
| **Metadata cross-referencing** | A PDF's "last modified by" field says `M.Chen`, and a LinkedIn search for "M Chen" at the target company returns exactly one match — identity confirmed. |
| **Infrastructure clustering** | Three "unrelated" domains all present the same self-signed SSL certificate fingerprint — revealing they're actually hosted on the same internal server. |
| **Timeline reconstruction** | Wayback snapshots + a GitHub repo's commit history + a LinkedIn "started new position" post all line up to the same week — confirming exactly when a new system went live. |
| **Negative space** | A former employee's GitHub repo containing the company's deployment scripts was deleted last month — right after a public vulnerability disclosure. The *deletion itself* is a signal worth noting in the report. |

