# 0x07 — OPSEC FOR THE INVESTIGATOR

- **Sock puppet accounts** — never use your personal/work identity to interact with target-adjacent platforms.
- **VPN/VPS egress** — route active scanning through infrastructure that isn't tied back to you (and is documented in your ROE/scope agreement).
- **Browser isolation** — use a dedicated, cookie-clean browser profile (or VM) for OSINT work so your own tracking cookies/fingerprint don't leak into results or tip off the target via analytics.
- **Rate-limit yourself** — aggressive dorking/scraping can get your IP flagged or banned by the platform, burning the lead.
- **Never escalate scope on your own** — a passive engagement finding something "interesting" is not authorization to actively scan it. Go back to the client/scope document.

